samltest-shibboleth.xml is a real SAML Response captured from samltest.dev.
It is public test data: the subject is john.doe@example.com and the signing
certificate is the samltest.dev "dummyidp" self-signed certificate.

The .exc goldens were produced by lxml (libxml2) exclusive canonicalization,
independently of this plugin's implementation:

  assertion.exc   the referenced Assertion after the enveloped-signature
                  transform removed its ds:Signature
  signedinfo.exc  the ds:SignedInfo element

Toolchain:
  lxml 6.1.1.0 libxml2 2.14.6
  OpenSSL 3.6.3 9 Jun 2026 (Library: OpenSSL 3.6.3 9 Jun 2026)

Verified before committing:
  sha256(assertion.exc) base64 == the message's own ds:DigestValue
  openssl dgst -sha256 -verify <cert pubkey> -signature <SignatureValue> signedinfo.exc  ->  Verified OK

  pubkey.spki.b64  the certificate's RSA public key in SPKI form, produced by
                   `openssl x509 -pubkey -noout`, so the spec can verify with
                   WebCrypto instead of pulling Node crypto types into a
                   browser package.
